Authentication Tests
----------------------
Unit Test:

usernameValidation
accepts all lowercase usernames, rejects all uppercase/number/other usernames

passwordValidation
accepts passwords only of length 5 or more

createCredentialsCreatesFile
Creating credentials creates a (non-empty) .cip file

createCredentialsRejectsBadInput
Invalid user or password will throw TopSecretException and doesn't create file

credentialsCheckStoredPair
Correct user + password passes, all other combinations fail

failsWithNoFile
Can't verify without a .cip file

ChangePasswordOverwrites
Changing the password/username replaces the .cip file

---------------------------------------
Integration Tests:
---------------------------------------

fullFirstRunCanBeValidated
After setting up credentials, the validation will work on a later login

passwordChangePropagates
A password change updates throughout the system, the new password works, the old one doesn't, and the file remains ciphered